{"schema_version":1,"id":"closure-20261110","generated_from":"IMPROVE TOR and HIPS tables, gallery/review/closeout_20261107/continuum_baseline.json, filters.json, spartan_reference.json and the unified filter dataset via research/ftir_hips_chem/workflows/run_addis_reference_closure_20261110.py","colors":{"Bega":"#E67E22","Belg":"#27AE60","Kiremt":"#3498DB","all sites":"#22252A","sites with median OC/EC < 4":"#2C6E9E","six urban sites":"#B23327","PM2.5 mass (gravimetric)":"#27AE60","Potassium (XRF)":"#2C6E9E","FTIR EC, SPARTAN published":"#B23327","HIPS Fabs":"#5B5852","measured":"#C49442","predicted from IMPROVE thermal EC":"#8a8f98"},"text":{"intro":"Which measurement carries the Addis offset: an answer to the question the 9 Nov status page left open, from data already in\nhand (233 Addis filters of the 7 Nov closeout, and the IMPROVE record of thermal EC and HIPS). **The aethalometer is not used**: the\nAddis MA350 is not a reference. A results page, not a recorded meeting. Exploratory: no Addis filter has thermal (TOR) EC, so the absolute\nlevel stays a range. Written account: docs/addis-reference-closure-2026-11-10.md.","improve":"**IMPROVE's own thermal EC shows HIPS falling behind as the filter darkens.** 347,936 IMPROVE samples\n(210 sites, 2005-2025) have TOR EC and HIPS on the same day. Grouped by the previous sample's EC loading at the site,\nso that neither instrument's error decides the group, HIPS Fabs ÷ TOR EC falls from 13.1 m²/g on the\nlightest filters to 8.4 at optical depth 0.94. A saturating curve through the group\nmedians has a **ceiling of 2.26** (1.82–2.70, resampling sites); the low-OC/EC sites and\nthe six urban sites give the same. Addis optical depth has a median of 0.96 and reaches 1.51, so\nAddis sits on the bend. No FTIR and no aethalometer enter this.","addis":"**At Addis, HIPS and FTIR EC are far from proportional, and the IMPROVE curve predicts most of it.** HIPS rises as FTIR EC\nto the power 0.46 (instrument: gravimetric PM2.5) or 0.41\n(XRF potassium); with no instrument at all the exponent is bounded to 0.39–0.54. If FTIR EC were exactly proportional\nto EC, the IMPROVE curve predicts 0.56 (0.46–0.64)\nat Addis optical depths. So HIPS compression accounts for most of the departure from 1. What is left over is small and not resolved:\na ceiling at the low end of its interval, or FTIR EC rising a little faster than EC. 233 Addis filters; 188 with\nPM2.5 mass, 189 with a published EC.","response":"**Linearising HIPS with the IMPROVE ceiling takes the intercept to zero.** The published fit moves from\n2.31x − 6.17 to **0.55x +0.01**\n(intercept +1.59 to -0.97 across the ceiling's interval). The correction is large\n(median × 1.74) and multiplies noise on the heaviest filters. Against linearised HIPS, FTIR EC is close to\nproportional but not exactly: linearised HIPS rises as FTIR EC to the power 0.85\n(0.78–0.92). The slope that remains is the level question: FTIR EC would\nneed a MAC near 19 m²/g to agree.","season":"**Most of the seasonal swing was HIPS; a smaller one remains, and lot 248 reads low.** Against HIPS as measured, FTIR EC ÷ HIPS\ngoes from 0.84 in Bega to 1.29 in Kiremt within lot 251. Against\nlinearised HIPS it goes from 0.51 to 0.60. Kiremt\nalso has the heaviest filters, so season and loading cannot be told apart here. Lot 248 reads lower than lot 251 in the same season\nagainst linearised HIPS (0.40 vs 0.51 in Bega) and\nagainst PM2.5 mass (0.16 vs 0.20), so that offset is not a HIPS effect.","level":"**What is left for FTIR is mainly one level factor, bracketed at about × 1.0 to 1.5.** Linearised HIPS needs\n18.7 m²/g to agree with the published EC. MACs measured with thermal EC are lower: 13.1 m²/g\nacross IMPROVE on light filters, 16.4 at the urban sites, about 19 on the\nfive Adama filters. Those put published ÷ true between 0.70 and 1.15. On held-out IMPROVE sites the calibration also reads\nthermal EC lower the lower the OC/EC (0.99 above OC/EC 4, 0.64 below 1.5; Addis FTIR OC/EC is\n1.34). Mass closure caps it: published EC reconstructs 89 % of gravimetric PM2.5, × 1.5 reaches\n100 % and × 1.9 gives 108 %. None of this is thermal EC measured at Addis.","network":"**The IMPROVE curve predicts the pattern across SPARTAN.** The exponent of HIPS against FTIR EC (instrument: PM2.5 mass) falls\nwith a site's optical depth about as the IMPROVE thermal curve says it should: near 1 at light sites, 0.69 measured\nagainst 0.62 predicted at Dhaka, and 0.46 against 0.57 at\nAddis, the heaviest site. Sites where the interval is wider than 0.6 are left off (11 of 23). The two Chilean sites sit\nfar below the prediction and need a second look before anyone quotes them.","next":"**Proposed position.** Carry the published FTIR EC forward with no intercept correction and a stated level range. Stop using\nFabs / 10 as the Addis yardstick without linearising. A modest season or loading effect and a lot-248 offset remain open. The proposed TOR\npass band (0.8 to 1.25) sits where the existing evidence predicts the answer (about 0.65 to 1.0), so ten filters would most likely read\n\"inconclusive\": decide before they arrive whether the deliverable is pass or fail, or an estimated level factor, and ask for HIPS on the\nsame filters with a few loaded to Addis optical depth. Optical agreement is still not thermal EC."},"tables":{"strata":{"population":["all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","all sites","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median OC/EC < 4","sites with median 